<title>MEXICO: Mexico outlines oilseed plantings, output forecast.</title>
<headline>Mexico outlines oilseed plantings, output forecast.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The local offices of the American Soybean Association (ASA) and United Soybean Board (USB) detailed Thursday national plantings for oilseeds and forecast productions levels for the 1997 harvest.</p>
<p>  Oilseed	 Hectares	   Seed Tonnage    Oil Tonnage</p>
<p>  Soybeans	 10,000		12,000	     2,160</p>
<p>  Safflower	81,354	     120,000	    45,600</p>
<p>  Cotton	    N/A		 350,000	    57,750</p>
<p>  Coconut	   N/A		 240,000	   120,000</p>
<p>  Corn		N/A		   N/A		25,000</p>
<p>  Total	     N/A		   N/A	     250,510</p>
<p>The ASA said the soybean projection was its own estimate and added that most plantings will be in Tamaulipas, although with some acreage in Chiapas and Chihuahua states.</p>
<p>Other oilseed outlooks were provided by the Guadalajara Oilseeds Crushers' Association, they added.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530)) E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
